      "writtenOn": "2023-05-02T20:30:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe we should document a convention here? Even with it documented, I suppose a client could add an extra e.g. \"PNG\" decoder when we already have a \"png\" decoder. I guess with it being appended to the end of the list, that doesn\u0027t help them accomplish anything.\n\nThough we could have a convention that we always convert to lower case (for example), meaning they would get what they probably wanted (replacing the existing one), but a client could always add \"png1\" or something. But the lower case convention would at least help us prevent users from accidentally adding a decoder that doesn\u0027t do anything.",
      "revId": "7667bb4dae93e84397abd3d7f038c83797da56f5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ababac5_3893e585",
        "filename": "include/codec/SkCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1025,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-02T20:48:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does this convention sound?\n\n\"By convention, we use all lowercase letters and go with the primary filename extension. For example \"png\", \"jpg\", \"ico\", \"webp\", etc\"",
      "parentUuid": "4818711d_6bafa98e",
      "revId": "7667bb4dae93e84397abd3d7f038c83797da56f5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
